- Release flags (T1, issue #20).  The optimized build kept its assertions:
  neither Make.config nor the flags of the C++ toolchain said -DNDEBUG, so
  libcyrt.so imported __assert_fail (401 call sites) and so did every
  generated module (3,610 in the Prelude, 45 in Fib); every call between
  translation units of the runtime, and every call from a module into the
  runtime, went through the procedure linkage table (4,188 PLT calls in the
  runtime, 49,582 in the Prelude); and the stack protector was on (313 call
  sites in the runtime).  Done: the optimized flavor in the Make.config
  template of configure adds -DNDEBUG -fno-stack-protector -fno-plt
  -fno-semantic-interposition, and libcyrt.so links with
  -Wl,-Bsymbolic-functions; the debug flavor (make DEBUG=1) keeps the
  assertions.  The flavor reaches the installation as sysconfig/cxx_flavor
  (config.cxx_flavor), and the C++ toolchain compiles generated modules in
  the same flavor (toolchain.FLAVOR_FLAGS: the flags above with -O3, and
  -Wl,-Bsymbolic-functions for every module) unless the interpreter flag
  debug is set.  The ABI stamp is a digest of the headers and of the flavor
  flags now (toolchain.object_digest), so a change to either compiles every
  object again, once: the prebuild of make stage for the library, the first
  import for a cache.  An object of the debug flag carries the debug digest;
  a session without the flag compiles it again, a session with the flag
  keeps it beside the objects of the installation (Cpp2So.accepted_digests).
  The objects depend on Make.config (src/Make.depends), and make warns once
  when configure is newer than Make.config: a tree with an older Make.config
  needs ./configure again.  The assert audit found no assertion with a side
  effect among the 153 of the runtime (the two rv.second patterns already
  cast rv to void), and the build with -DNDEBUG gives no warning.  After the
  change, libcyrt.so and the Prelude import neither __assert_fail nor
  __stack_chk_fail and make one PLT call each (__cxa_finalize).  Measured
  with the harness (C++ backend, three repetitions, CPU seconds, ratio new
  over old; steps equal): Tak1 7.21 to 6.27 (0.87), Fib 1.14 to 1.00
  (0.88), Queens10 6.70 to 5.82 (0.87), Reverse 1.92 to 1.80 (0.94),
  Primes 9.39 to 8.00 (0.85); peak RSS unchanged.  Tests:
  unit_cxx_toolchain.py (TestFlavor: the installed runtime and the Prelude
