- Cheap Variable (T2, issue #21).  Every argument access in a step built a
  Variable with two heap-backed vectors (the path from the root of the step
  and the set guards crossed), so the step of fibgen called operator delete
  18 times and the out-of-line constructor of Variable three times, and a
  nested access (_1[1]) moved the vectors again.  Done: SmallVec
  (cyrt/smallvec.hpp), a sequence with inline room for N plain values and a
  heap block beyond it; Variable keeps its path in a SmallVec of 8 entries
  and its guards in one of 2, and stays 64 bytes.  The heap block comes
  from two helpers of the runtime library (smallvec_alloc, smallvec_free),
  and the growth step is out of line, so a generated module imports no
  allocator for its variables.  The indexer moved from indexing.cpp to
  indexing.hxx, included from node.hxx, so the constructor, operator[], and
  rvalue are inline: a plain successor costs a few loads and one store into
  the inline path; a forward node of one link is shortened in place; only a
  longer chain calls compress_fwd_chain, and only a variable with guards
  calls guarded_rvalue.  operator[] copies the lists of the parent and
  appends, instead of a vector insert at the front; the order of the
  entries is as before (the path of the parent first, the guards of the
  parent last).  The show of the guards prints the set addresses instead of
  "{TODO}".  Found on the way: the front end lifts every level of a nested
  pattern into a function of its own (unwrap__CASE0 ...), so no variable of
  the Prelude or of the benchmarks has a path of more than two entries; the
  inline room is left only through set guards.  Also, with the release
  flags of T1, the known defect of a set function whose value is a sub-term
  of its argument (above, 2026-10-03) is no longer an abort but an endless
  loop: hnf and procD say assert(0); continue; at T_SETGRD.  Measured with
  the harness (C++ backend, three repetitions, CPU seconds, ratio new over
  old; steps equal, peak RSS unchanged): Tak1 6.26 to 3.75 (0.60), Fib 1.02
  to 0.81 (0.80), Queens10 5.84 to 4.58 (0.78), PermSort 12.23 to 11.16
  (0.91), Reverse 1.81 to 1.01 (0.56), Primes 8.35 to 6.06 (0.73), Psort
  38.77 to 23.38 (0.60).  Static: the step functions of Fib.so and Tak1.so
  call no operator new, operator delete, malloc, or free (objdump); their
  call targets are node_reserve, node_commit, compress_fwd_chain,
  guarded_rvalue, the cold grow of SmallVec, and the never-taken
  smallvec_free of the destructor.  Tests: unit_cxx_variable.py
  (TestSmallVec: a C++ program, data/cxx/smallvec_test.cpp, compiled
  against the installed runtime: inline room, growth, copies and moves in
  both directions, self-assignment, append, equality, pointer values, and
