  functions, whose innermost match carries three guards).  Left: W3 of the
  throughput note (plain pointers for pass-through arguments) would remove
  the Variable of an argument that is only passed on; the T_SETGRD loop in
  hnf and procD needs an error instead of assert(0).
- Alias inlining (T3, issue #22).  The Prelude's instance methods for Int
  arithmetic and comparison are aliases: i1 <= i2 = ltEqInt i1 i2, and the
  +, -, and * wrappers forward to plusInt, minusInt, and timesInt.  A call
  of one cost a rewrite step and a node before the call of the external it
  forwards to; four of the ten steps of a call of tak in Tak1 were such
  forwards.  Done: the optimizer pass inline_aliases (interpreter/optimize.py;
  the analysis in icurry/analysis/aliases.py).  An alias is a function whose
  body is one saturated call of another function on exactly its own
  parameters, in order.  The pass runs last, per function, when a module is
  loaded, so it reaches the generated code of both backends and leaves the
  FlatCurry-to-ICurry translation alone (the oracle: 1196 equal, 0
  different).  It replaces each IFCall of an alias by a call of the end of
  the chain of aliases, through the loaded modules; a partial application
  keeps the alias as its head; the alias function itself stays.  Each alias
  records its direct target under the metadata key all.alias_target, which
  both backends write into the module (the C++ Metadata variant takes the
  string), so a module loaded from its compiled form still tells its aliases
  to the modules that import it.  A target may be private to its module
  (both backends resolve a symbol through the symbol table of its module,
  and the C++ backend exports every info table) or external (the call
  becomes the call of the built-in).  When the target lives in a module the
  caller does not import, the module joins the imports, so the C++ link
  line and the Python import list carry it.  A chain that closes on itself,
  a target of another arity, and a target that is not loaded leave the call
  alone.  The optimizers are called as optimizer(interp, ifun, imodule) now.
  Cached generated code: the C++ format stamp went from 2 to 3, and the
  Python emitter got the same stamp (# FORMAT: 2 on line 2 of a generated
  file; Json2Py refuses a file of another stamp or of none, and a file
  without a stamp is format 1), so make stage and the first import write
  every cached module again, once.  The Prelude has 23 aliases; its own
